.TH AR09 1 2026-11-11 "bcc09 0.13.1" "bcc09 Manual"
.SH NAME
ar09 \- make and change libraries (archives) of object files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ar09
.RB [ \- ]\c
.IR key " [" position "] " archive
.RI [ file ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ar09
keeps object files from
.BR as09 (1)
together in an archive, a library that
.BR ld09 (1)
links the members of that a program needs.
It is the Free Software Foundation's ar of 1988, as dev86 has it.
.PP
The
.I key
is one operation letter, with modifier letters after it.
.SH OPERATIONS
.TP
.B r
Put the files in the archive, replacing members of the same names (made
if there is no archive).
.TP
.B q
Append the files to the archive quickly, without looking for members of
the same names.
.TP
.B d
Delete the members named.
.TP
.B x
Extract the members named (all of them if none is).
.TP
.B t
List the members (those named, or all).
.TP
.B p
Print the members' contents on standard output.
.TP
.B m
Move the members named, in the order named, to the end of the archive
(or to
.IR position ,
with
.BR a ,
.B b
or
.BR i ).
.SH MODIFIERS
.TP
.B a
Put new or moved members after the member
.IR position .
.TP
.BR b ", " i
Put them before
.IR position .
.TP
.B c
Make the archive without saying so.
.TP
.B u
With
.BR r ,
replace only members older than their files.
.TP
.B o
With
.BR x ,
give the files the dates the members have.
.TP
.B s
Accepted and ignored:
.B ld09
needs no symbol table in an archive (it reads every member's symbols).
Alone, as
.BR ranlib 's
job, it only checks that the archive is there.
.TP
.B v
Say what is done to each member.
.TP
.B l
Accepted and ignored.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 if all went well, 1 otherwise.
.SH EXAMPLES
A library of three objects, then its members:
.PP
.RS
.nf
ar09 rc libmine.a one.o two.o three.o
ar09 t libmine.a
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bcc09 (1),
.BR as09 (1),
.BR ld09 (1),
.BR objdump09 (1)
